---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy | Echo"
  description="Privacy for the Echo website and the Echo browser extension. The website uses cookieless analytics; the app and extension send nothing to the project."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated 1 November 2026.</p>

    <h2>The Echo app and browser extension</h2>
    <p>
      Echo is software you run on your own Mac. The project does not operate any service for it and
      never receives your recordings, transcripts, notes, settings or usage data. The app and the
      extension contain no analytics, telemetry or crash reporting.
    </p>
    <p>
      The browser extension reads only the meeting sites you enable (Google Meet, Zoom web and
      Microsoft Teams web) to detect an open meeting and your mute state. It captures audio only
      after you start a recording, keeps it encrypted in your browser, and sends it only to the Echo
      server running on your own computer. It does not use your camera, and it does not sell,
      transfer or share any data with anyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      The full list of network requests the app can make is in the
      <a href="/docs/privacy/">documentation</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      echo-web.samarthmn.com is a static site hosted on Vercel. It uses Vercel Web Analytics, which
      counts page views without cookies and does not track you across sites. Vercel, as the host,
      processes standard request data such as IP addresses to serve and protect the site. There are
      no forms, accounts or advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/samarthmn/echo-voice-web/issues">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
